index 0000000..90c8be8
--- /dev/null
+++ b/crates/vp-protocol/tests/SS_VERIFICATION.md
@@ -0,0 +1,94 @@
+# Shadowsocks standards repair / verification tranche
+
+Scope: four legacy AEAD methods and the three SIP022 methods. This tranche is
+protocol implementation plus same-implementation regression evidence, **not a
+release certification or independent full-program interop pass**.
+
+Primary sources checked on 2026-10-30:
+- https://shadowsocks.org/doc/aead.html
+- https://shadowsocks.org/doc/sip022.html
+- https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-shadowsocks/blob/65740e0f0e3e/shadowaead/protocol.go
+- https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-shadowsocks/blob/65740e0f0e3e/shadowaead_2022/protocol.go
+- https://github.com/SagerNet/sing-box/blob/v1.14.4/go.mod
+
+The product uses existing RustCrypto AES/GCM and XChaCha20Poly1305 primitives,
+HKDF-SHA1 and BLAKE3 derive-key mode; no custom cipher is introduced. XChaCha is
+no longer silently aliased to 12-byte-nonce ChaCha. Legacy UDP uses one zero-nonce
+AEAD record. SIP022 has standalone directional TCP headers, request-salt response
+association, 30-second timestamps, exact 60-second TCP salt replay retention,
+AES separate-header UDP / XChaCha UDP, session-ID routing and 1024-packet exact
+sliding replay windows. UDP state advances only after authentication, direction,
+time, address and client-session association validation. UDP sessions live 300
+seconds after valid incoming traffic; full caches fail closed rather than evict
+live replay state. TCP initial headers are bounded by a 10-second timeout.
+
+Stream fixes also cover authenticated early data, legacy 0x3fff / SIP022 0xffff
+chunk limits, transport half-close, authentication errors (not silent EOF), nonce
+exhaustion and backpressure without duplicate input. The shared relay pump must
+flush accepted buffered output: that fix is supplied by the P09 baseline and is
+not copied into this exclusive protocol patch. SS TCP/UDP listener tasks and
+connection work now use its task scope. UDP response work is separately tracked;
+listener-owned JoinSets await handles rather than aborting in-flight replies when
+ingress stops.
+
+## Executed locally, Rust 1.88.0, on P09 baseline
+
+Baseline `73d1bc8d5073168572c0306937da154c3a6e00c9`. The only standalone lock
+change is adding the existing locked `socket2` dependency edge to `vp-protocol`;
+no crate version or checksum changes. The one-line manifest edge is coordinated
+with the core integration owner.
+
+```
+cargo +1.88.0 test -p vp-crypto --lib --locked
+cargo +1.88.0 test -p vp-protocol --test ss_standard --test ss_managed --test ss_library_interop --locked
+cargo +1.88.0 test -p vp-protocol --test udp ss_udp_loopback --locked
+cargo +1.88.0 test -p vp-protocol --lib ss::tests::ss_ --locked
+cargo +1.88.0 test -p vp-protocol --lib snell::tests --locked
+```
+
+- Crypto: 24 passed; 2 existing captured-VMess-fixture tests ignored.
+- P09 core lifecycle/relay regression baseline: 18 passed.
+- `ss_standard`: ten passed. Includes seven-method TCP 180KB+half-close and UDP
+  sizes 0/128/4096; wrong-key/type/timestamp/padding/replay target absence; corrupted
+  UDP target absence; SS2022 session mobility; response association; invalid
+  association cannot poison the replay window; seven-byte duplex backpressure.
+- `ss_managed`: three passed. Established TCP finishes during drain (zero forced
+  tasks), partial handshakes cancel promptly, actual TCP/UDP ports rebind after
+  shutdown, connection tables empty, and IPv4/IPv6 UDP replies still arrive during
+  drain while new ingress is blocked. UDP has no EOF: idle associations are forcibly
+  canceled at the configured drain deadline, with zero tasks remaining and the
+  single outgoing dual-stack port released. This bounded forced cleanup is reported,
+  not mislabeled as a naturally drained UDP session.
+- Existing SS UDP regression: one passed. Existing SS TCP regressions: two passed.
+- Snell shared-codec regressions: six passed.
+- `ss_library_interop`: Rust harness compiles; **two tests intentionally ignored**.
+  Go module download, dependency integrity verification, build and execution are
+  pending the separately requested authorization. There is no generated go.sum
+  and no invented hash or successful reference result.
+
+## Remaining release gates / explicit limits
+
+1. The official sing-box 1.14.4 and 1.10.7 CLIs are blocked at network-manager
+   initialization by sandbox netlink restrictions, before listening. That is not
+   a cipher failure or pass. No network-policy bypass is attempted. The prepared
+   test-only official-library peer is a distinct evidence tier, never a production
+   replacement engine.
+2. Run both directions of the seven-cipher TCP/UDP matrix and wrong-key target
+   absence after authorized official Go setup; retain the exact resolved go.sum,
+   compiler/build identities and actual logs. Unsupported reference behavior is
+   a gap, never a pass.
+3. Mixed-family UDP is now implemented with one explicit dual-stack socket and
+   verified against live IPv4/IPv6 loopback targets for all seven methods, including
+   one shared source port and mapped-address canonicalization. On hosts without
+   dual-stack support IPv4 may fall back explicitly; IPv6 capability is not claimed.
+   The endpoint-restricted reply policy only returns datagrams from a requested
+   target, with 64 active target endpoints/session. Unsolicited sources and a 65th
+   target are dropped, without evicting established destinations/replay state.
+   Non-Linux/native-platform dual-stack behavior remains unverified.
+4. Legacy salt replay memory is bounded to 60 seconds and does not confer SIP022's
+   full session-bound replay guarantees. SIP023 multi-user identity headers are
+   not implemented; the ordinary single-PSK SIP022 construction is the scope here.
+5. Server SIP022 probe handling selects zero-linger reset behavior on accepted TCP
+   sockets. Platform-specific packet-level probe behavior and native OS lifecycle
+   acceptance remain unverified. Scoped listener/task cancellation and bounded
+   drain are locally verified against P09; preserve those wrappers on replay.
