@@ -0,0 +1,25 @@
+# Official Shadowsocks protocol-library peer (test-only)
+
+This adapter calls unmodified `sing-shadowsocks` pinned to the dependency revision
+of official sing-box **v1.14.4** (`65740e0f0e3e`) and its resolved `sing` revision.
+It does not reimplement Shadowsocks framing, authentication or cryptography.
+All listeners, dial targets and plaintext echo targets are constrained to loopback.
+The adapter deliberately does not instantiate sing-box NetworkManager, whose
+netlink initialization is blocked in this sandbox. Results are protocol-library
+interop, **not** a full sing-box executable integration pass.
+
+Credentials arrive via stdin and exist only for the child process lifetime.
+No installer, route, firewall, system-proxy, TUN or persistent-key operation exists.
+The Go module is a test dependency, never a production engine or runtime fallback.
+
+Build only after authorization for the official Go compiler and library fixture:
+
+```
+go mod tidy
+go mod verify
+go build -trimpath -o reference-ss .
+VP_SS_REFERENCE=/absolute/path/reference-ss cargo test --locked -p vp-protocol --test ss_library_interop -- --ignored --nocapture
+```
+
+Preserve actual `go.sum`, compiler version and binary/dependency hashes in evidence.
+The Rust matrix tests both directions, seven ciphers and TCP/UDP independently.
